the public&#x02019;s response to a bioterrorist attack.</article-title><source>J Health Commun</source> <year>2003</year>;<volume>8</volume>(<issue>Suppl 1</issue>):<fpage>83</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>92</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14692573</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Keeter</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Miller</surname> <given-names>C</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Kohut</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Groves</surname> <given-names>RM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Presser</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Consequences of reducing non-response in a national telephone survey.</article-title><source>Public Opin Q</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>64</volume>:<fpage>125</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>48</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/317759</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10984330</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Curtin</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Presser</surname> <given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Singer</surname> <given-names>E</given-names></string-name> <article-title>The effect of response rate changes on the Index of Consumer Sentiment.</article-title><source>Public Opin Q</source> <year>2000</year>;<volume>64</volume>:<fpage>413</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>28</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/318638</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11171024</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Traugott</surname> <given-names>MW</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Assessing poll performance in the 2000 campaign.</article-title><source>Public Opin Q</source> <year>2001</year>;<vo